# === Resend (email service for the contact form) ===
# Get your API key here: https://resend.com/api-keys

RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# === SENDER + RECIPIENT (set these AFTER domain verification) ===
# See KONTAKT-FORM-PROBLEM-OG-LOESNING.md for the full guide and domain move steps.
#
# After you have verified højfynsspartel.dk in Resend:
# - You can send FROM any address on the verified domain.
# - You can send TO any email address you want.
#
# Recommended (professional):
# Use Punycode (ASCII) for the actual email address part to avoid "Invalid 'from' field. The email address contains non-ASCII characters." in Resend.
# Display name can have unicode characters.
# Punycode for højfynsspartel.dk: xn--hjfynsspartel-bnb.dk
#   (compute with: node -e "console.log(require('punycode').toASCII('højfynsspartel.dk'))" )
#
# In Vercel UI (Environment Variables > edit sensitive var):
# - For CONTACT_FROM Value field, type/paste exactly (no quotes):
#   Højfynsspartel <info@xn--hjfynsspartel-bnb.dk>
# - For CONTACT_TO Value field, type/paste exactly:
#   info@xn--hjfynsspartel-bnb.dk
#
# Note: In Vercel edit for Sensitive vars, the current value is hidden (blank field). You must re-enter the full value to save/update.
# Copy-paste should work, but type it if copy-paste fails in the UI.
# (Your email provider should accept delivery to the Punycode or Unicode form of the address.)
#
# IMPORTANT: Make sure you actually have a working inbox for the CONTACT_TO address.
# Resend only *sends* the email. Receiving happens via your normal email provider
# (the one that handles MX records for højfynsspartel.dk).

# (Historical note: Previously fell back to test mode with onboarding@ and fastfun50@gmail.com.
# Now that CONTACT_FROM / CONTACT_TO are set with Punycode, no fallback is needed.
# If missing, the code will log an error and likely fail the send.)
